From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:35:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 46/48] app-list: take no space when the taskbar shows every
 app

With the taskbar running, the App List hides each app the taskbar
shows. When every favourite is running and every window is in the
taskbar, both lists are empty and upstream draws its own icon instead.
That icon is not a button, so the panel showed an App List icon that
did nothing when clicked.

Draw nothing in that case: the applet shrinks to one pixel and comes
back as soon as it has an item to show (a favourite closes, or a window
is not in the taskbar). Without the taskbar the App List keeps
upstream's icon.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

